Energy refund after Burst can work in well-batteried teams, but usually require more ER than Sacrificial. More effective with refinements and consistent Skill casts. R3+ preferred."}],"a":[{"names":["Emblem of Severed Fate"],"text":"His best general set: 20% ER and Burst DMG scaling with ER directly support his main damage source.","stats":"ER/ATK% · Hydro DMG · CRIT"},{"names":["Noblesse Oblige"],"text":"Provides a teamwide ATK buff after Burst if nobody else is using Noblesse, at the cost of personal damage.","stats":"ER/ATK% · Hydro DMG · CRIT"},{"names":["Noblesse Oblige","Heart of Depth"],"text":"Mixed Burst and Hydro DMG bonuses are an easy temporary option before farming a strong 4-piece Emblem set.","stats":"ER/ATK% · Hydro DMG · CRIT"}],"t":[{"name":"National Book Club","members":["Xingqiu","Xiangling","Bennett","Sucrose"],"text":"Xingqiu supplies Hydro for Xiangling Vaporize; Bennett buffs and batteries, while Sucrose groups and shares EM.","roles":["Sub DPS","Off-field DPS","Buffer / Healer","Anemo Support"]},{"name":"Raiden National","members":["Xingqiu","Raiden Shogun","Xiangling","Bennett"],"text":"Raiden recharges the team and drives Xingqiu sword rains; Xiangling Vaporizes while Bennett buffs both damage dealers.","roles":["Sub DPS","Driver / Battery","Off-field DPS","Buffer / Healer"]},{"name":"Rain Sword Hyperbloom","members":["Xingqiu","Nahida","Kuki Shinobu","Alhaitham"],"text":"Xingqiu creates Bloom cores with Nahida and Alhaitham; Kuki triggers Hyperbloom while healing the team.","roles":["Hydro Enabler","Dendro Support","Hyperbloom Trigger / Healer","Main DPS"]},{"name":"Double Hydro Vaporize","members":["Xingqiu","Hu Tao","Yelan","Zhongli"],"text":"Xingqiu and Yelan maintain Hydro for Hu Tao Vaporize while Zhongli protects her and shreds resistance.","roles":["Hydro Enabler","Main DPS","Sub DPS","Shield Support"]}],"v":"High Energy Needs: Use Sacrificial Sword R3+ or Favonius, ER Sands as needed, and enough ER to Burst each rotation.\nC6 Low 